  "headline": "Grim stays clear as Paul Ray storms Gameweek 8",
  "summary": "Louis Grimoldby remains top on 563 despite a João Pedro captaincy blank, with Mark Horton 28 points back on 535. Paul Ray was the Gameweek 8 star with 51 points for This my year FC, while olly barnes climbed to third and sits just 1 point ahead of Will Finney.",
  "report": "Louis Grimoldby and Grim FC remain in command after Gameweek 8, holding 563 points and a 28-point lead over Mark Horton’s Vespa Mo Pedro on 535. It was not all plain sailing for the leader: Louis handed the captaincy to João Pedro, who returned 0. Still, 38 net points kept Grim FC at the summit, and Louis is also the league’s hottest manager over the last three gameweeks with 189 net points.\n\nMark Horton posted 34 to retain second, with the reliable Haaland captaincy bringing 8 points at a multiplier of 2. Haaland was the overwhelming captaincy favourite, selected by 18 managers and owned by 23, or 88.5% of the league. Behind Mark, olly barnes rose two places into third after scoring 37 for Grasshoppers, reaching 529 points. Will Finney’s 33 leaves 0v3rf1tt3d.h5 on 528, just 1 point behind olly, while Tim Chodha slipped two places to fifth after a 20-point week.\n\nManager of the week belongs to Paul Ray. This my year FC delivered 51 points with no hits, the best score in the BFL and 19.8 points above the league average of 31.2. Paul’s four-place rise was the biggest climb of the week, ahead of Callum Bowness, up three with 41, and Jamie Mitchell, also up three with 37. George Foy’s 46 and Vaughan Cosbie-Ross’s 42 completed the week’s top three scores.\n\nThe differentials came out to play. Abi Speight had BOU’s Hill for 11, while Ali Smith owned both FUL’s Bobb and NEW’s Dedić, each worth 11. Phil Johnson’s BOU defender Truffert supplied 10, James Marshall got 10 from LEE goalkeeper Trafford, and Jamie Mitchell found 9 points from LIV’s Isak. Ali’s squad had another twist, though: 20 points were left on the bench, the week’s bench-agony crown.\n\nAt the other end, Dan Birkinshaw’s MadjoKarp collected the wooden spoon with 11 and fell three places. Chris Beeden and David Tonks each scored 17 and dropped four places, the largest falls of Gameweek 8. Georg Coakley remains the coldest manager across the last three gameweeks on 121 net points.\n\nThere were no chips played and no hits taken, so this was a straight shoot-out. With 30 gameweeks remaining, the lead is intact but the race behind Louis is tightening: Mark leads olly by 6, olly leads Will by 1, and George Foy holds a 4-point advantage over Mike Flynn in the battle for sixth. Mark’s 116 in Gameweek 2 remains the season record, but Paul Ray’s 51 was the statement score of Gameweek 8.",
